<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Tahir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Tahir was the head of the Banu Tahir, a local family who took effective control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> in the 11th century. Murcia had been governed for the Amirid rulers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, but under him the family ruled as patricians, nominally under Valencia, drawing wealth from the irrigated farmland of the Segura valley.</p></div>
